      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "NEAL K. KATYAL, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nJEFFREY B. WALL, Principal Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, in support of reversal.\nTHOMAS J. O'CONNOR, ESQ., Albany, New York; On behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Edward G. McDonough)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: McDonough's Section 1983 suit claimed that Smith brought and maintained criminal proceedings against him based on fabricated evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Katyal, is your claim allege a -- require the finding of probable cause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I'm pretty sure they don't swim at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: What torts would you bring -- tort suits would you bring under state law under -- on these facts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If Petitioner were seeking damages for a conviction based on fabricated evidence, it is clear under Heck malicious prosecution would be the most analogous common law tort, and favorable termination would be an element of the 1983 claim. That's Heck itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So it's always an element now? Before, it was sometimes an element. But now it's always an element?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So -- but the -- what -- the problem is that the Petitioner says it's not making that claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. O'CONNOR: It's hard to say what claim the Petitioner is making. It -- it started out with -- with two claims, a malicious prosecution claim and a fabrication of evidence claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The malicious prosecution claim was dismissed. The Second Circuit affirmed the dismissal and it -- the dismissal remains unchallenged."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: It's a presumption, but in this case, if you let people to bring lawsuits while a criminal trial is going on at the same time, they're bringing a civil lawsuit against some of the people who are heavily involved in the case, and you're -- you're going to mix up many cases, and people will watch what they say or -- who knows."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. O'CONNOR: -- in limited circumstances, for example, where, although there is sufficient evidence to satisfy probable cause, the 1983 plaintiff alleges that there is unrelated independent evidence that is fabricated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. O'CONNOR: Well, let me -- in this case, after the -- after the defendant was acquitted in this case, he had two years and three months to file this action in a timely manner, embracing both of the claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "295c6e85cd63d90ecbdf3ab5dd05b20fb68ec490db4d58913c2706e8943d3f64",
      "evidence_id": "ev-295c6e85cd63-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: You do say something in your brief, I think, that was puzzling. You say that an acquittal at trial means that the use of false testimony at that trial didn't deprive him of liberty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2018-18-485",
